  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="256">
        <pb n="293"/>
        <head>256 — i — II. — <quote>Thou hast shaken the earth and opened it</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">Again Hymns on the Earthquakes on the 7th of the Month of September in the Year 562 (513).</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">Lord<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> who hast stretched out the heaven<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> like a curtain, and holdest in the palm of thy almighty<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> right hand the earth and all the ends thereof, who by thy commandment<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> didst gather<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> the waters of the seas into one heap [and supportest<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> all things by the word of thy power and rulest them as God, do not, my Lord, by threatening and [applying to us the punishment that our sins deserve<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> dissolve and destroy the compact order that governs thy creation, and condemn us to the sentence of bitter death by earthquake; but [according to the mercy of thy kindness<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> turn toward us and save us; for in thee [we live and move and exist<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a10" target="#n10" n="10"/>, merciful Lord.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 1</orig></choice> Ps. lx, 4.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 2</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>Thou</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 3</orig></choice> Ps. civ, 5 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>powerful in all</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 5</orig></choice> Heb. i, 3 <quote>Is the brightness..... all things by the word of his power. And he..... for our sins</quote> (verbal diff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 6</orig></choice> Gen. i, 9.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>who bearest</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 8</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>punishing the disorderliness of our sins</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 9</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>in the mercy of thy clemency</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 293, n. 10</orig></choice> Acts xvii, 27, 28 Harkl. <quote>That they might be seeking God, if perchance they might feel him and find him; although he is not far from each one of us; for in him we live and move and exist</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
